<title>HONG KONG: Oxford Properties H1 profit down 28 pct.</title>
<headline>Oxford Properties H1 profit down 28 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended July 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   36.6  vs 50.9</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    12.0  vs 12.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    24.79 vs 34.49</p>
<p>    Turnover		     44.78 vs 54.53</p>
<p>    Company name		 Oxford Properties &amp; Finance Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  November 15-22</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   December 9</p>
<p>NOTE - Oxford is a property and share investment firm.</p>
<p>The company paid no special cash bonus per share vs three H.K. cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
